<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE BY ONE CENT/LITRE.</title>
<headline>DUTCH SHELL CUTS DIESEL PRICE BY ONE CENT/LITRE.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-07-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Royal Dutch/Shell unit Shell Nederland BV said on Thursday it would cut its retail prices for diesel in the Netherlands by one cent per litre with effect from Saturday, July 12.</p>
<p>The move reflects changes in international product prices and the value of the dollar against the guilder, the company said. It added that gasoline prices would remain unchanged.</p>
<p>From Saturday, the price of diesel at Shell's self-service stations will fall to 1.506 guilders per litre.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000</p>
